ual-copy and size-type configuration-LP values both equal $B$, but whose integral optimum is greater than $B+c$. Distinguishing a packing in $B$ bins from the absence of one in $B+c$ bins is NP-hard for each fixed $c$. A deterministic polynomial-time algorithm with a fixed absolute additive allowance exists exactly when $P=NP$; under that equality, an optimal algorithm is constructed.","title":"Bin packing and unbounded configuration-LP gaps","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/docs/118.md"}},"provenance":{"kind":"computed-navigation","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","rule":"Projection of the pinned ledger; no new mathematical assessment."},"reader_comparison":{"headline_coverage":"agree","method":"Compare reported scope categories; notes remain attributed and are not adjudicated.","points":[{"definitions_to_check":null,"gap":null,"note":null,"reading":"reading:6d2c0feb9d8875bc0ec504bd","source_term":"MATCHES","state":"all"},{"definitions_to_check":"`PEqualsNP := ClassP = ClassNP` with `ClassP` via `TM2ComputableInPolyTime` deciders (+ finite alphabet) and `ClassNP` via `CookLevin.InNP` certificate verifiers; LP values are `sInf` over fractional covers (nonempty, bounded below)","gap":null,"note":"None; P/NP are defined by Mathlib TM2 poly-time deciders and the certificate definition (`InNP`).","reading":"reading:50f8931f73c3f1ca898a594d","source_term":"full","state":"all"}],"readings":["reading:6d2c0feb9d8875bc0ec504bd","reading:50f8931f73c3f1ca898a594d"],"state":"agree"},"readings":[{"availability":"recorded","credit":{"atlas_pin":"f047bac96ee80ebef0b4f5a403831b84de6e32c1","authors":[{"handle":"carlostoledo1891","name":"Carlos Toledo"}],"kind":"third-party-reported","license":"MIT","method":"Every Comparator challenge re-run on Linux with nanoda switched on, decided by a preregistered rule; every family's challenge statements read against OpenAI's hea